    {
      "symbol": "DraggableScrollableState",
      "option": "initial_child_size",
      "default": "required, starting and reset fraction",
      "validation": "mount starts here; reset restores here with pristine flags",
      "comparison": {
        "prose": "Mount and reset share the initial value; replacement preserves the live size instead of re-applying it. Delivery is FIFO in commit order to every listener through a sheet-owned drain: nested commits enqueue behind in-flight events, so the reset event precedes any reentrant events and never arrives delayed past newer state (inner listeners still observe the committed sheet). Payloads describe their own commit; listeners read extent() for live state. At sheet-notify time only the inner restore is still pending, so sheet-listener inner moves are overwritten while sheet-extent changes survive; at inner-notify time nothing is pending. No sheet-extent state mutates after callbacks begin, so nested resets see committed state.",
        "refs": [
          {
            "path": "crates/incular-widgets/src/advanced_scrolling/draggable.rs",
            "kind": "method",
            "owner": "DraggableScrollableState",
            "name": "reset"
